The Security Council,

Recalling its resolutions 2235 (2015) of 7 August 2015 and 2319 (2016) of 17 November 2016,

1. Decides to renew the mandate of the Joint Investigative Mechanism, as set out in resolution 2235 (2015), for a period of 30 days from the date of adoption of this resolution;

2. Takes note of the different views expressed by members of the Security Council on the Joint Investigative Mechanism;

3. Requests the Secretary-General to present to the Security Council, within 20 days of the adoption of this resolution, proposals for the structure and methodology of the Joint Investigative Mechanism, reflecting the views of Council members;

4. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

The Security Council,

Recalling its resolutions 2235 (2015) of 7 August 2015 and 2319 (2016) of 17 November 2016,

Stressing the importance of maintaining the unity of the Security Council on the issue of Syrian chemical weapons,

1. Decides to renew the mandate of the Joint Investigative Mechanism, as set out in resolution 2235 (2015), for a period of 30 days from the date of adoption of this resolution;

2. Takes note of the different views expressed by members of the Security Council on the Joint Investigative Mechanism;

3. Requests the Secretary-General to present to the Security Council, within 20 days of the adoption of this resolution, proposals for the structure and methodology of the Joint Investigative Mechanism, reflecting the views of Council members, with a view to ensuring that it conducts comprehensive, objective, and impartial investigations, while fully preserving the independence and professional integrity of the Joint Investigative Mechanism in accordance with resolution 2235 (2015);

4. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

The Security Council,

Recalling its resolutions 2235 (2015) of 7 August 2015 and 2319 (2016) of 17 November 2016,

Stressing the importance of maintaining the unity of the Security Council on the issue of Syrian chemical weapons,

1. Decides to renew the mandate of the Joint Investigative Mechanism, as set out in resolution 2235 (2015), for a period of 30 days from the date of adoption of this resolution;

2. Takes note of the different views expressed by members of the Security Council on the Joint Investigative Mechanism;

3. Requests the Secretary-General to present to the Security Council, within 20 days of the adoption of this resolution, proposals for the structure and methodology of the Joint Investigative Mechanism, reflecting the views of Council members, with a view to improving its working methods and ensuring that it conducts comprehensive, objective, and impartial investigations based on solid evidence, while fully preserving the independence and professional integrity of the Joint Investigative Mechanism in accordance with resolution 2235 (2015);

4. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

